hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"987","Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, Ibn Abi Adi, Muhammad bin Ja’far, Sahl bin Yusuf, and Abd al-Wahhab bin Abd al-Majid told us. Al-Thaqafi, they said: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Raja, Imran bin Husayn narrated to us, he said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, one night we traveled until dawn came before dawn, and we had that event, and there is no event more beautiful for a traveler than this. Nothing woke us up except the heat of the sun, and so-and-so was the first to wake up, then so-and-so called them Abu Raja’, and Awf called them, then Omar was the fourth. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept, we did not wake him until he was awake, because we do not know what would happen to him in his sleep. When he woke up, Omar Ibn Al-Khattab saw what happened to the people. He was a hollow, icy man. He said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his voice with “Allahu Akbar.” He continued to say “Allahu Akbar” and raised his voice. Until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was awakened by his voice. When he woke up, they complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had struck them. He said: “There is no harm or no harm. They set out, so they set out and he walked not far away, then he descended and called for water and performed ablution, then he called for prayer and led the people in prayer.”"
